Intelligent car mimic the flight of bumblebees
Which would the best way to avoid accident avoidance if the obstacle-desensors wouldn’t impersonate from each other?
For example bees.
An amazing project was introduced at CEATEC in Japanese where the Nissan engineers were inspired by bumblebees during the completion of new accident-avoiding systems.
In cooperation with the Tokyo university, Nissan has built BR23C biomimetic system, controlled by automotive robots, a mini-car equipped equipped with bees' characteristics, with the aim of supporting the development of a system that avoids any collision.
Kazuhhiro Doi said Kazuhhiro Doi, product manager for technology PR and research engineering at the exhibition.
The composed view of the bee, which can be seen in every direction and an angle of more agony above 300 degrees, plays an important piece.
To imitate the function of the combined view, the researchers took up the concept of the laser-controlled distance meter.
It identifies obstacles before BR23C in a panoramic field of 180 degrees within 2 meters, calculates its distances and sends signals to the microprocessor on board, which immediately initiates collision-avoiding process.
The obstacle is registered in fractual units of a year-fraction, the auto robot immediately changes course, similar to the movement of bees by rotating tires around an appropriate corner.
In contrast to previous systems this manoeuvre takes place purely instinctive.
"Unfortunate if it weren't enough, the car robot couldn't react quick enough to avoid obstacles," said Toshiyuki Andoh, head of the "Mobility laboratory" and car robot project.
The system must react instinctively and immediately, because this technique corresponds to the most intimate and wilful part of the shield - a shift in which accidents are currently unavoidable.
The entire process must reflect bees behavior when avoiding other bees.
This has to happen in a split second.
Nevertheless, in contrast to the bees, the evasion may occur not up, down, or even diagonal - it can only be two-speed, only in the direction of the usufluggability of the tires.
Whereas bees have an infinite number of possibilities to avoid other bees here, the researchers could only use the rotary movement respectively acceleration and deceleration.
The BR23C includes lithium polymer batteries, which are lighter and more energy-efficient and therefore have a longer service life than conventional lithium-ion batteries.
Andoh said it comes down the instinctive, intelligent response, rather than the processing of data, and even less on the ability to save it.
This device simply need a few inputs per second and respond accordingly.
It don't necessarily necessary to save them, or use previous manoeuvres to produce an intuitive, logical reaction, meaning that it constantly only occupies a hand-full KB memory.
It does not require giga-by-byte and mega-byte-heavy memories.
This is the initial step in developing immediate collision avoidance technology, which, according to estimation from Nissan, will in production within the next ten few years.
An other application could include GPS satellite navigation technology by consciously guiding driving drivers around obstacles, thus moving him at their destination.
