Different possibilities are available: ocean power, for example, takes advantage of a system of connected buoy.
The thrust of the waves, which moves buoyons up and down, is converted into hydraulic pressure within the floats via pistons and cylinder.
It drives a turbine, which in turn operates a generator.
The electricity is sent to the coast via underwater pipes.
